    "narrative": "Our optimal lineup for May 10th centers on a trio of high-upside plays, led by **Lawrence Butler** (73.47), who benefits significantly from a 16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Chris Bassitt. **Taylor Ward** (70.00) and **Bryson Stott** (68.39) join him as our strongest starters; **Taylor Ward** thrives on that same park-driven offensive environment against Luis Severino, while **Bryson Stott** draws a massive 18% lift from the SP skill profile of Tomoyuki Sugano. **Brendan Donovan** also merits attention; though his base is modest, his leadoff spot (10% bonus) and platoon advantage against Davis Martin push him to a 65.57 score, making him a high-floor engine for our Roto categories today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Geraldo Perdomo**, who finished at 54.66, narrowly missing the cut behind the superior platoon and park metrics of our starting outfielders. While **Geraldo Perdomo** remains a viable depth piece, the optimizer favored the efficiency of **Wenceel Perez** (60.68) and **Masyn Winn** (59.99), the latter of whom remains a priority start due to the potential for stolen bases against Walker Buehler\u2019s slower delivery. We remain cautious regarding the \u201cLineup Pending\u201d status for several players, particularly **Will Smith** and **Cal Raleigh**; should they shift down in the batting order, their efficiency scores will adjust downward, potentially narrowing the gap between them and the bench options like **Matt Chapman** or **Gavin Sheets**. We are currently avoiding **Tyler Freeman** entirely, as his matchup against the elite 2.96 xERA of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez suppresses his value below our acceptable threshold for today's roster.",
